rem Linear Combinations of Semiprimes
rem https://projecteuler.net/problem=278
rem Sum f(p q r) over primes p < q < r
rem below Limit, f(n) being the greatest
rem number not a sum of multiples of
rem p q, p r and q r

use numbers
use sequences
use io
use cli

option Limit integer = 5000

rem For these primes f = 2 p q r - p q -
rem p r - q r. Summed over all triples,
rem p q r gives the third elementary
rem symmetric sum e3 of the primes, and
rem the pairs each occur with the m - 2
rem other primes. The sums e2 and e3
rem come from the power sums.
Ps = primes till Limit array
M = Ps len
S1 = Ps sum
S2 = (Ps * Ps) sum
S3 = (Ps * Ps * Ps) sum
E2 = (S1 * S1 - S2) // 2
Cube = S1 * S1 * S1 - 3 * S1 * S2
E3 = (Cube + 2 * S3) // 6
Answer = 2 * E3 - (M - 2) * E2
Answer print
